agent_3.revised_operationalization:
1. At the start of each day, the moderator calculates 25% of the lake’s current stock and writes that number into the ledger as "daily_limit_kg".
2. Each fisher reads "daily_limit_kg" from the ledger, multiplies it by 30% and records their personal cap as "personal_cap_kg".
3. During the day each fisher logs the amount they have caught under "harvested_kg".
4. After logging, the moderator compares each fisher’s "harvested_kg" to their "personal_cap_kg".
5. If "harvested_kg" exceeds the cap, the moderator:
   a) returns the excess kilograms to the lake and updates the lake stock;
   b) reduces the fisher’s "harvested_kg" by 1 kg;
   c) subtracts the value of 1 kg – taken from the ledger entry "price_per_kg" – from the fisher’s payoff;
   d) records a fine of 1 kg in the ledger as "fine_kg".
6. The fisher’s payoff is then calculated based on the adjusted "harvested_kg" and the current "price_per_kg".
